        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "faa63944-cb9a-55df-9462-64c8b9dbd57d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Walton, John Wooden, Brad Nessler, Tom Tolbert, Lucious Harris\n- Organizations: UCLA Bruins, UCLA, Nets, ABC, NCAA\n- Events: 2002 NBA Finals, 2003 NBA Finals\n- Topics: college basketball, NCAA national championships, sports broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton became known playing for John Wooden's UCLA Bruins powerhouse team.\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton won three successive College Player of the Year Awards and led the UCLA Bruins to two Division I national titles.\n- John Wooden, nicknamed the \"Wizard of Westwood,\" won ten NCAA national championships in 12 years as UCLA head coach, including a record seven consecutive titles.\n- Lucious Harris played in the 2002 NBA Finals and the 2003 NBA Finals as a member of the Nets.\n- The 2003 NBA Finals were broadcast on ABC in the United States, with Brad Nessler, Bill Walton, and Tom Tolbert as announcers.",
